---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const pageViewsEnabled = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PAGE_VIEWS_ENABLED === 'true';
---

<BaseLayout title="Imprint" description="Legal information and privacy policy">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8" style="view-transition-name: page-title;">Imprint</h1>

    <div class="prose">
        <h2>
            Information according to § 5 TMG and Responsible for the content
            according to § 18 Abs. 2 MStV
        </h2>

        <p>
            Niklas Heer<br />
            <!-- TODO: Verify address is current -->
            Uzstraße 18<br />
            D-91522 Ansbach
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>

        <p>
            E-Mail: <a href="mailto:me@nheer.io">me@nheer.io</a>
        </p>

        <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>

        {pageViewsEnabled ? <>
        <p>
            This site uses Vercel Web Analytics to count page views and display
            each page's total. Vercel processes aggregate traffic information,
            including the page visited, referring site, browser, device and
            approximate location. The integration removes URL query parameters
            and fragments before sending page views.
        </p>
        <p>
            Vercel Web Analytics uses no third-party tracking cookies. Its visitor identifier
            expires after 24 hours. Public counters show page views, not unique
            people, and may update with a delay. For details, see
            <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy">Vercel's analytics privacy documentation</a>.
        </p>
        </> : <>
        <p>
            Out of a long tradition of interest and deep love for data
            protection, we inform you in our privacy policy that we do not want
            to know who you are if you find yourself on this website. We also
            don't want to know how long you stay here, what you look at or even
            which website you visit afterwards.
        </p>

        <p>
            Because your behaviour on our website is none of our business, we do
            not collect any data about your user behaviour and do not record
            server logs.
        </p>
        </>}

        <p>
            Data protection always begins and ends with personal data. Because
            the question when data is personal is so important, the European
            legislator has inserted a legal definition for this in Art. 4 Lit.1
            GDPR:
        </p>

        <blockquote>
            "Personal data" means any information relating to an identified or
            identifiable natural person ("data subject"); an identifiable
            natural person is one who can be identified directly or indirectly,
            in particular by reference to an identifier such as a name, an
            identification number, location data, an online identifier or to one
            or more specific characteristics that express the physical,
            physiological, genetic, psychological, economic, cultural or social
            identity of that natural person.
        </blockquote>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
